From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 06:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] galliumglue: emit m68k trampolines

The GalliumCoreAPI glue routes every Mesa-core call a pipe driver makes through
a module-local table, so driver and core can be redeployed independently. The
routing is done with one assembly trampoline per imported function, and the
generator knew two architectures:

    ap.add_argument("--arch", default="arm", choices=("arm", "aarch64"),

which is the whole of what stood between this and a VC4 Gallium driver on
m68k. Everything else was already in place: Mesa 20.0.8 unpacks and builds for
this target, libmesa.a and libgalliumauxiliary.a are there, and softpipe and
i915 build as Gallium drivers alongside.

The m68k trampoline is two instructions, and transparent for the same reason
the ARM one is -- nothing but a call-clobbered scratch register is touched, so
varargs, struct returns and FP arguments pass through untouched:

    move.l __gca_local+N,%a0
    jmp (%a0)

a0 and a1 are call-clobbered on m68k and the SysV m68k ABI passes every
argument on the stack, so no argument can be sitting in the register the
trampoline uses. Absolute addressing rather than a GOT, since the table is in
the same module.

166 trampolines come out for libgallium_vc4.a.
---
--- a/workbench/libs/mesa/galliumglue.py
+++ b/workbench/libs/mesa/galliumglue.py
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
                     help="data symbols resolved by extracting the defining "
                          "provider member into the consumer module")
     ap.add_argument("--mesa-version", required=True)
-    ap.add_argument("--arch", default="arm", choices=("arm", "aarch64"),
+    ap.add_argument("--arch", default="arm", choices=("arm", "aarch64", "m68k"),
                     help="target CPU: picks the trampoline template")
     ap.add_argument("--abi-flags", default="",
                     help="ABI-relevant compile flags; part of the hash so "
@@ -304,6 +304,20 @@
             s_.append("    ldr ip, 0f")            # ip = &__gca_local
             s_.append("    ldr pc, [ip, #%d]" % (i * 4))
             s_.append("0:  .word __gca_local\n")
+    elif args.arch == "m68k":
+        s_.append("    .text\n")
+        for i, s in enumerate(funcs):
+            s_.append("    .balign 2")
+            s_.append("    .globl __gca_%s" % s)
+            s_.append("    .type __gca_%s, %%function" % s)
+            s_.append("__gca_%s:" % s)
+            # a0 and a1 are call-clobbered on m68k and no argument arrives
+            # in a register -- the SysV m68k ABI passes everything on the
+            # stack -- so loading through a0 is as transparent here as ip is
+            # on ARM. Absolute addressing, no GOT: the table is in the same
+            # module.
+            s_.append("    move.l __gca_local+%d,%%a0" % (i * 4))
+            s_.append("    jmp (%a0)\n")
     else:   # aarch64
         s_.append("    .text\n")
         for i, s in enumerate(funcs):
